 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Legislature clause:** general seats in the legislature to be shared on an **equal district-wise basis** between the regions."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Gentlemen's Agreement (20 Feb 1956):** Andhra side led by Andhra State CM **Bezawada Gopala Reddy** (with N. Sanjiva Reddy); Telangana side led by **B. Ramakrishna Rao**."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 7,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Rajaji as Premier (1937):** left **Rayalaseema out of his cabinet**; later made anti-Andhra statements."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 8,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **JVP report and Dhar:** the JVP Committee **reaffirmed the Dhar Commission's approach** – security, unity and economic prosperity first, new linguistic provinces postponed."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Legacy:** its regional safeguards became a **model for the Gentlemen's Agreement (1956)**."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 6,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Today:** its terms on the **capital, High Court and irrigation** are still cited in Rayalaseema debates (e.g. a High Court at Kurnool)."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 8,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Dhar Commission's mandate:** to examine the formation of **Andhra, Karnataka, Kerala and Maharashtra**, with their boundaries and consequences; Gujarat was not in its terms."
  },
  {
   "book": 1,
   "row": 255,
   "sec": 12,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Gandhi in Hyderabad:** visited Hyderabad on **9 March 1934** during his Harijan tour."
  }
 ],
